WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:07.049
To impress my fling, I had a threesome experience with him and his friend. I absolutely hated it and regret continuing it for seven hours.

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:30.419
Once when I was in tenth grade, I dated a girl because I felt bad for her.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:36.660
But I was not attracted to her at all. I realized that I was leading her on, so broke off the relationship.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.960
She has major trust issues and hasn't dated anyone since then. It's been nine years.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.450
I was out with my kids in the mall and bumped into an ex flame. Being a single mother I flirted with him

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.459
but when he asked me if the kids are mine

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.460
I lied to him and said they were my sister's.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.380
My kids heard that and asked me if I won't be taking them back home with me. It broke my heart.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:06.780
I think it's hard for me to empathize with that just because like I'm so excited for the day that I have kids.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.019
I do understand not wanting to be judged

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.349
and wanting to be seen a certain way by someone.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:19.350
When I was 11, I got into a relationship with a guy I met online who claimed he was 16.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.379
I was planning on going to meet him, but my parents stopped me.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.710
I found out later that he led his next victim to commit suicide.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.350
Well this kind of

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.439
hits a little close to home for me.

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:34.499
Meeting people online kind of helped

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:41.069
my self-esteem because it made me feel like oh this person doesn't even know me and they want to talk to me and it makes

00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:46.060
you feel like you're pretty and you're worthy. You don't actually need that validation.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.180
It's kind of just got to come from yourself. Not some random man on the Internet.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:51.470
 

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.470
I am a married woman

00:01:53.720 --> 00:02:00.249
but I am still in love with my first boyfriend. I don't think I love anyone like I loved him.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.479
Sometimes I imagine him when I'm making love to my husband.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.860
That is interesting and also I think...

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:18.100
It is- it is pretty sad. I'm about to get married and from time to time

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.700
I do think about

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.840
like past

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.920
relationships and I, I don't necessarily think of them in the light of like I wish I was still in them just more on a

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.580
reflective side of things, but I think you should probably

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:37.869
question why you're in the relationship you're in, right? And like, if you still really love like your husband

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:43.689
it might be something that you guys can actually work through together even if it's hard.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:48.339
My ex-husband told me that he was abused by his father when he was a teenager.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.920
I saw abusive tendencies in him as well

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.189
but I stayed with him for six years because I was sure I could change him.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.660
But after having our son he finally did it - he gave me a black eye.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:04.959
My biggest regret was ignoring all the red flags because not having my ex around has brought me so much relief.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.650
Yeah, oof.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.469
Yeah, it's kind of this like hope that you're clinging on to that

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.680
like we'll make a difference right, you know hoping that someone would change

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:21.500
and a lot of times it's so heartbreaking because the reality is sometimes people don't change. And I also

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.969
would urge this person to not be so hard on themselves.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.509
Because you know where they were coming from was such a place of love and compassion. It just turned out that you

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.890
know this person maybe wasn't ready for it.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:42.439
I had an abusive ex-boyfriend and adopted three cats with him in an attempt to improve our relationship.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.680
One weekend after staying with my mother

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:52.730
I returned home to find that he had purposely killed our three cats to punish me for having gone for the entire weekend.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.420
I called the police and have a restraining order for him.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.650
But I was with him for so long and it terrifies me. Oh my gosh

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.410
How do you

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.389
help somebody in that situation? How do y- what can you tell them to make them feel better?

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.020
You know

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.429
you kind of get yourself out and you leave and you do what's best for you and you know to whoever

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.560
this is from, I'm proud of them.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:21.679
When my husband's parents divorced last year his dad stopped talking to him.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:29.420
I told my husband that it was his dad's job to reach out first. A few weeks later his dad committed suicide.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:37.370
I regret ever saying anything, maybe if I stayed quiet my partner would have spoke to his father and things could have been different.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.380
Our time with other people is not a given thing.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.399
It closes saying "maybe if I stayed quiet

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.770
my partner would have spoke to the father", but it's also possible that person might have

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:01.490
taken the same approach and waited for the father to contact. So I advise people from...

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:10.340
Not to be overly critical with themselves at times, even though this is a grave tragic situation. But um...

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:18.140
I'm a 19 year old woman who has never fallen in love before, and I had never really identified to any particular

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:23.620
sexuality. When my best friend told me that she was in love with me, it made me feel amazing.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:28.760
I wanted to be honest, so I told her that I wasn't sure she said she would wait for me and after six months

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.960
I said yes, but one week later, I broke up with her because I realized I wasn't gay.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:41.840
I felt so guilty, confused and ashamed but the experience made me better understand who I was and more accepting of my mistakes.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:45.720
Yeah, I know what it feels like to

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:49.840
both love someone who doesn't love you back and

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:55.120
also to be on the receiving end of someone's feelings and not be able to reciprocate them.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.130
And I think both of them can actually feel really terrible.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:05.030
Sometimes the easy decision is to say yes, okay, let's date. But if it's not right and if you feel that in your core then

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.750
it's

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:13.280
more harmful to us actually, so sometimes the most loving thing that we can do to someone else is actually be honest with them.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.840
I let my emotionally abusive boyfriend influence my college choice.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:24.499
I chose a small local college over an Ivy League because he was afraid that I'd become more pretentious in a bigger college.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.040
Fuck that guy

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.210
damn.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:37.129
It sounds like they were going for something and the boyfriend was afraid that you know, she would become a little too...

00:06:38.639 --> 00:06:43.609
Good for him. And if that's the case and people want to prevent you from being your best good self I say

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.280
it's okay to outgrow people.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.640
Like I'm very sorry that you know this abusive boyfriend

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.840
was that manipulative because that should never happen to anybody. But on the other end of it

00:06:55.849 --> 00:07:01.819
I think this probably can be a huge opportunity for this person to realize how much power they have. And like,

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:05.400
you know, be able to choose for themselves.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.820
I hope that there's a discovery of that power, or there has been for this person.

